    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output 4.4. Increased capacity of member States and enterprises to develop policies and measures that promote the alignment of business practices with decent work and a human-centred approach to the future of work</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">4.4.1: Government of Khyber Pukhtunkhwa adopts new Industrial Policy and Strategy with focus on Decent Work, and aligned with human-centred approach to the future of work.

4.4.1: The Terms of Reference of the national focal point for Promoting the MNE Declaration  in Pakistan was agreed at the tripartite meeting of the ILO constituents in December 2020. The representatives of the Ministry of Overseas Pakistanis and Human Resource Department (MOPHRD), Employers Federation of Pakistan (EFP), and Pakistan Workers Federation (PWF) attended the tripartite meeting. The meeting concluded with a tripartite agreement to nominate the Employers&#x2019; Federation of Pakistan as the national focal point for the promotion of the ILO MNE. This appointment is on a rotational basis - the EFP will serve as the focal point for a period of three years after which the role will be rotated among Workers and Government. 4.4.1:  The Industries Department of Khyber Pukhtunkhwa Province organized a detailed briefing for ILO  on their draft Industrial Policy and Strategy on 10th June 2021.  Subsequently, on 27th July 2021, ILO provided detailed technical inputs and shared a number of national and global publications and tools to align the draft Industrial Policy and Strategy with human-centred approach and principles of Decent work for the future of work.</narrative>
   </description>
